              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">defefdcb-5b0c-4031-ae54-ece97ccb7cd0</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">How to use this demo (Foton 0.3.8)
1. First time only: set install_ on Foton Settings to True and wait for it to finish.
2. Drag the Room sliders. Daylight autonomy on the floor updates as you drag.
3. Toggle Neighbour block and move it closer. Turn on Daylight factor to see it on the plan beside the room (each slider move then takes a little longer).
4. Press Save run to write a results folder and compare Foton with Honeybee.
Blue groups are Foton's own components (HB-Foton tab), green ones Ladybug Tools, orange ones only belong to this demo. Needs Ladybug Tools.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
