                        <chunk name="OutputParam" index="1">
                          <items count="6">
                            <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Daylight autonomy results in percent. DA is the percentage of occupied hours
that each sensor recieves equal or more than the illuminance threshold.
Each value is for a different sensor of the grid. These can be plugged
into the "LB Spatial Heatmap" component along with meshes of the sensor
grids to visualize results. These can also be connected to the "HB
Spatial Daylight Autonomy" component to compute spatial daylight
autonomy for each grid.</item>
                            <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">71c9e367-5f73-44fe-91e6-ed761944c0cf</item>
                            <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">DA</item>
